  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Gobind Narayan vs The State Of Jharkhand ..... Opposite ... on 10 June, 2022 Author: Deepak Roshan Bench: Deepak Roshan 1 In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi Cr. Revision No. 763 of 2004 Gobind Narayan ..... Petitioner Versus The State of Jharkhand ..... Opposite Party ---------",
    "facts": "The prosecution case in brief is that Sri M.N. Mallick, the then Food Inspector Hazaribagh submitted prosecution report duly certified by the Additional Chief Medical Officer, Hazaribagh alleging therein that he visited the Kirana shop of accused persons on 25.09.1986 for inspection and during his inspection he suspected that Arhar Dal and wheat flours are adulterated and not fit for consumption. As such he collected sample as per rules and sent it to the public analyst who reported vide report No. 2580, dated 05.11.1986 that the Arhar Dal was adulterated. He requested for prosecution, accordingly the cognizance was taken. Petitiioners were summoned in pursuance of which they appeared. Thereafter, a charge for offence under Section 16 (1) a (1) of the P.F.A. Act was Gobind Narayan vs The State Of Jharkhand ..... Opposite ... on 10 June, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/165595505/ 1 framed against the accused persons on 16.06.1989 for which they pleaded not guilty and claimed to be tried. After trial they were convicted by the trial court. The petitioner also lost in appeal.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioner confines his argument on the question of sentence and submits that the petitioner remained in custody for about 65 days and he is aged about 62 years and during entire period of bail, he never misused the privilege of bail, as such the sentence may be modified. 5. Learned counsel for the State supported the judgment and submits that there is no error in the findings given by the Courts below. As such, the conviction cannot be [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioner confines his argument on the question of sentence and submits that the petitioner remained in custody for about 65 days and he is aged about 62 years and during entire period of bail, he never misused the privilege of bail, as such the sentence may be modified. 5.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Learned counsel for the State supported the judgment and submits that there is no error in the findings given by the Courts below. As such, the conviction cannot be [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
